<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. above consolidated financial results of Company have been reviewed by Audit Committee and approved by Board of Directors ofCompany in their respective meetings held on June 9,2020 (through video conferencing).  nThe consolidated financial results are prepared in accordance with Indian Accounting Standards                     (“Ind AS”), as applicable and guidelines issued by the “SEBI”. Ind AS are prescribed under section 133 of Act read with Rule 3 of the Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Rules, 2015, and Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) (Amendment)Rules, 2016. The said financial results represent the results of PSP Projects Limited (“the Company”), its subsidiaries (together referred to as “the Group” and its share in results of joint ventures which have been prepared in accordance with Ind-AS 110 – “Consolidated Financial Statement”  and Ind AS 28 –“Investment in Associates and Joint Ventures”).  n2.Group has adopted Ind AS 116, “Leases”, effective April 1, 2019 using modified retrospective method in respect of its leases. adoption of this standard does not have any material impact onfinancial result.  n3.outbreak of COVID-19 pandemic globally and in India is causing significant disturbance and slowdown of economic activity. Group’s management believes while COVID-19 may adversely impact on the business in short term, it does not anticipate material medium to long term risk to business prospects.   nGroup has made detailed assessment of it’s liquidity position for the next year and the  recoverability of Group’s assets such as Trade receivables, Unbilled revenue, Investments, Inventories,Advances, etc as at the Balance Sheet date, using reasonably available information, estimates and judgements, and has determined none of these balances requires material adjustments to their carrying value. impact of COVID-19 may be different from that estimated at the date of approval of these financial results and the Company will continue to closely monitor the developments.  n4.Group has elected to exercise the option permitted under section 115BAA of the Income Tax Act -1961 as introduced by the Taxation Laws (Amendment) Ordinance 2019. Accordingly, Group has recognised tax expenses for the FY ended March 31, 2020 and re-measured its deferred tax assets basis rate prescribed in said section. Profit for the period is lower by rs 164.51 lakhs due to remeasurement of deferred tax assets recognised upto March 31, 2019.  n5.Group is primarily engaged in one business segment viz. construction/project activities, as determined by chief decision maker in accordance with Ind AS 108, Operating Segments. Further, operations of Company is predominately domiciled in India and so there are no reportable geographical segment.  n  nfor note 6 to 10- refer notes to assets liabilities</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
